1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:03,534
If you only have nineteen days of food, plant today.

2
00:00:04,134 --> 00:00:07,820
The Harvest. Part one of three. Nineteen days.

3
00:00:08,420 --> 00:00:15,341
Nineteen days of food. Forty-one mouths. Winter is sixty days away.

4
00:00:15,941 --> 00:00:18,665
Sack, sack, sack. Not enough sacks.

5
00:00:19,265 --> 00:00:25,001
My husband's seeds. Radish, lettuce, spinach. Seventeen years old.

6
00:00:25,301 --> 00:00:26,673
Do seeds expire?

7
00:00:26,973 --> 00:00:28,134
Only if you do.

8
00:00:28,734 --> 00:00:36,043
Radish, twenty-five days. Lettuce, thirty. Spinach, forty. Potatoes take months.

9
00:00:36,643 --> 00:00:38,831
Cook the seed potatoes! Eat now!

10
00:00:39,131 --> 00:00:42,475
Eat the seed, and next year you eat nothing.

11
00:00:43,075 --> 00:00:48,333
One seed eaten is one meal. One seed planted is many.

12
00:00:48,933 --> 00:00:51,686
Dig where the sun stays at least six hours.

13
00:00:52,713 --> 00:00:54,449
Frost comes in twenty-two days.

14
00:00:56,493 --> 00:00:58,638
That night, someone dug up the seed bed.

15
00:01:00,453 --> 00:01:04,594
Part one of three, The Harvest. Next: the rattle.
